      "message": "### Style Guide Cleanup: Chrono Literals\n\n**Rationale:** The Google C++ Style Guide bans `using namespace` directives inside `.h` header files to prevent global namespace pollution, but strongly encourages the use of standard literal suffixes (e.g., `5s`, `200ms`) in `.cc` implementation files for readability.\n\n**The Changes:**\n\n* Leave the explicit `std::chrono::milliseconds(5000)` declarations inside `bootrom.h` and `usb_interface.h` untouched.\n* In your `_test.cc` and `.cc` files (where `using namespace std::chrono_literals;` is already declared), swap out verbose constructors for literals.\n\n```cpp\n// Change this:\nEXPECT_EQ(fake_usb_.Receive({}, std::chrono::milliseconds(0)).error(), UsbError::kTimeout);\n\n// To this:\nEXPECT_EQ(fake_usb_.Receive({}, 0ms).error(), UsbError::kTimeout);\n\n```",
