      "message": "Additional feedback from Gemini:\n\n----\n\nHere are all the instances in the implementation (`.cc`) and test files where explicit `std::chrono` constructors should be replaced with literal suffixes.\n\nBecause both of these files already contain the `using namespace std::chrono_literals;` directive at the top of the file, making these changes is perfectly safe and aligns with the Google C++ Style Guide\u0027s preference for readability.\n\n---\n\n### 1. `bootrom_test.cc`\n\n**Location:** Inside the `SystemResetDoesNotWaitForResponse` test fixture.\n**Rationale:** Passing a zero-timeout explicitly can be shortened to `0ms`.\n\n**Before:**\n\n```cpp\nEXPECT_EQ(fake_usb_.Receive({}, std::chrono::milliseconds(0)).error(),\n          UsbError::kTimeout);\n\n```\n\n**After:**\n\n```cpp\nEXPECT_EQ(fake_usb_.Receive({}, 0ms).error(),\n          UsbError::kTimeout);\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `et171_flash.cc`\n\n**Location:** Inside the anonymous namespace at the top of the file used for bootloader configuration variables.\n**Rationale:** Standard literals (`5s` and `200ms`) make global or file-scoped configuration variables much easier to scan.\n\n**Before:**\n\n```cpp\nconstexpr auto kBootloaderConnectTimeout \u003d std::chrono::seconds(5);\nconstexpr auto kBootloaderConnectPollInterval \u003d std::chrono::milliseconds(200);\n\n```\n\n**After:**\n\n```cpp\nconstexpr auto kBootloaderConnectTimeout \u003d 5s;\nconstexpr auto kBootloaderConnectPollInterval \u003d 200ms;\n\n```\n\n---\n\n*(Note: The `std::chrono::milliseconds(...)` declarations inside `bootrom.h` and `usb_interface.h` remain untouched to strictly enforce the Google C++ Style Guide rule against using-directives in header files).*",
